{{!
    @template mod_selfselectadvanced/coresync_report

    The Moodle group mirroring status report (1.20.7 item 7b). Shows, per
    team, whether its mirrored course group exists and whether it is in step
    with the plugin roster, so staff can find a lagging or failed sync
    without reading cron logs.

    Membership counts only - no participant contact field appears here for
    any viewer, and the contact-privacy rule is unaffected by this page.

    filterhtml and tablehtml are Moodle-rendered form and table markup and
    are emitted RAW for that reason; every value inside them is escaped by
    the form and table APIs that produced them. Nothing else on this page
    takes the raw path.

    backurl is computed by the page from the viewer's capabilities - it
    points at the manager dashboard only for a holder of :manage, and at the
    activity otherwise, so a least-privilege auditor is never given a Back
    button to a page they cannot open.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * heading - the page heading
    * intro - one line explaining what the report shows
    * filterhtml - rendered filter form (raw Moodle form markup)
    * tablehtml - rendered results table (raw Moodle table markup)
    * backurl - where Back goes for this viewer
    * backlabel - the Back button's label

    Example context (json):
    {
        "heading": "Moodle group sync",
        "intro": "Every approved team and the state of its mirrored course group.",
        "filterhtml": "<form></form>",
        "tablehtml": "<table></table>",
        "backurl": "https://example.com/mod/selfselectadvanced/view.php?id=2",
        "backlabel": "Back to the activity"
    }
}}
<h2>{{heading}}</h2>
<div class="mb-3">{{intro}}</div>
<div class="mb-3">{{{filterhtml}}}</div>
{{{tablehtml}}}
<div class="mt-3">
    <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="{{backurl}}">{{backlabel}}</a>
</div>
